title: Case Manager › Active cases › A new case joins the tracker
route: /manager
intro: A case signed and sent in New case becomes a request on the Dashboard. The tracker adds it as a row marked 'New today', so the header count, the four status tiles, the pager and the rows always agree. A case that was already a row in the ledger (for example R-1042) keeps its row and gets no second one.
dir: TD
also: The new row follows the request. Fast-forward moves its clock. Reset demo data removes the row.
---
start s1 "New case › Review and sign › 'Sign and send'"
store st1 "A request is created on the Dashboard as Received\nIts ID is added to 'sent today'"
goto g1 "Continues in: Authorizations › New case › Review and sign › Sign and send"
decision d1 "Is the ID already a row in the tracker?\n(R-1042, R-0988, I-2207, R-1101, I-2262 are)"
process p1 "The row stays as it is"
process p2 "A tracker row is added\nCase ID with a green 'New today' tag, initials and age\nLevel of care and request type\n'not yet approved', payer, approval chance from the draft"
process p3 "Clock and status follow the request\nWith the payer: 'Decision expected in 2 h', 'Awaiting payer'\nInfo requested: 'Decision expected in 24 h', 'Needs action'\nApproved: Units or days '0 of 14 days used, 14 left', Next due '14 days left' (IOP: '24 units left'), 'On track'\nDenied: 'Window closes Fri', 'Needs action'"
process p4 "Header reads '57 active cases.'\nThe four tiles, 'Showing 1 to 10 of 57' and 'Clear them to see all 57' count it too\n'5 are still being prepared' drops by one"
click c1 "Click the row, the case ID or 'Open'"
goto g2 "Continues in: Authorizations › Case"
end e1 "Count, tiles and rows agree"

s1 --> st1 --> g1
st1 --> d1
d1 -->|Yes| p1 --> e1
d1 -->|No| p2 --> p3 --> p4 --> e1
p2 --> c1 --> g2
